1
00:03:13,846 --> 00:03:19,846
But not all dogs stay there!

2
00:06:27,692 --> 00:06:33,692
All Dogs Go to Heaven is a drama, animation, family film directed by Don Bluth.

3
00:09:41,538 --> 00:09:47,538
When a casino-owning dog named Charlie is murdered by his rival Carface, he finds
himself in Heaven basically by default since all dogs go to heaven.

4
00:12:55,384 --> 00:13:01,384
However, since he wants to get back at his killer, he cons his way back to
the living with the warning that doing that damns him to Hell.

5
00:16:09,230 --> 00:16:15,230
Once back, he teams with his old partner, Itchy, to prep his retaliation.

6
00:19:23,076 --> 00:19:29,076
He also stumbles onto an orphan girl who can talk to the animals, thus allowing him to
get the inside info on the races to ensure his wins to finance his plans.

7
00:22:36,923 --> 00:22:42,923
However, all the while, he is still haunted by nightmares of what's waiting for him on
the other side unless he can prove that he is worthy of Heaven again.

8
00:25:50,769 --> 00:25:56,769
Charlie B. Barkin (voice), played by Burt Reynolds.

9
00:29:04,615 --> 00:29:10,615
Itchy Itchiford (voice), played by Dom DeLuise.

10
00:32:18,461 --> 00:32:24,461
Anne-Marie (voice), played by Judith Barsi.

11
00:35:32,307 --> 00:35:38,307
Carface (voice), played by Vic Tayback.

12
00:38:46,153 --> 00:38:52,153
Whippet Angel (voice), played by Melba Moore.

13
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
King Gator (voice), played by Ken Page.

14
00:45:13,846 --> 00:45:19,846
All Dogs Go to Heaven is a 1989 animated musical fantasy comedy drama film directed by Don
Bluth and co-directed by Gary Goldman (his directorial debut) and Dan Kuenster.

15
00:48:27,692 --> 00:48:33,692
Set in New Orleans in 1939, it tells the story of Charlie B.

16
00:51:41,538 --> 00:51:47,538
Barkin (voiced by Burt Reynolds), a German Shepherd mix who is murdered by
his former friend, Carface Carruthers (voiced by Vic Tayback).

17
00:54:55,384 --> 00:55:01,384
Charlie escapes from Heaven to return to Earth where his best friend, Itchy Itchiford
(voiced by Dom DeLuise), still lives, in order to take revenge on Carface.

18
00:58:09,230 --> 00:58:15,230
Instead, he ends up befriending a young orphan girl named
Anne-Marie (voiced by Judith Barsi in her final film role).

19
01:01:23,076 --> 01:01:29,076
In the process, Charlie learns an important lesson
about kindness, friendship and love.

20
01:04:36,923 --> 01:04:42,923
The film is an Irish, British and American venture, produced by
Goldcrest Films and Sullivan Bluth Studios Ireland Limited.

21
01:07:50,769 --> 01:07:56,769
On its cinema release, it competed directly with Walt Disney Feature
Animation's The Little Mermaid, released on the same day.

22
01:11:04,615 --> 01:11:10,615
While it did not repeat the box-office success of Sullivan Bluth's previous features, An American Tail and The Land
Before Time, it was successful on home video, becoming one of the biggest-selling VHS releases ever.

23
01:14:18,461 --> 01:14:24,461
It was followed by a theatrical sequel, a television
series, and a holiday direct-to-video film.

24
01:17:32,307 --> 01:17:38,307
The film explores themes of new orleans, louisiana,
villain, heaven, little girl, dog.

25
01:20:46,153 --> 01:20:52,153
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
